  "id": "DrugBank_DB00387 - MONDO_10709",
  "verbalization": "Procyclidine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Procyclidine is associated with Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, a condition that is linked to the same syndrome through different medications. Pimavanserin and Istradefylline, both indicated for Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, are also linked to the same syndrome, indicating a potential shared pathophysiological mechanism. The presence of these indications suggests that Procyclidine may exert a role in the development of this syndrome through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood, possibly involving neurodegenerative processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in the evaluation of drug-repurposing strategies for this condition. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
